WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
Grow algae in two nutrient
solutions that are identical,

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:06.910
except that one has
only half the phosphate.

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.120
Use five flasks of each.

4
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.780
Then plot the mean number
of cells as two bars.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.770
One bar reaches 48.

6
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.970
The other reaches 44.

7
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.130
On paper, a difference.

8
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:23.500
So when does a difference between
two bars actually mean something?

9
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.340
In this mission, you'll see what
the top of each bar really shows:

10
00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.850
not every result, but a mean.

11
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.130
Then you'll meet the thin
lines drawn on top of bars,

12
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.510
and find out why the first
thing to read is the legend.

13
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.480
Your mission: find out when a difference
between two bars actually means something.
